      "rationale": "The mount surface — editor/viewer app ids, the OS artifact kind id, the inference tool id, the window roster, the on-disk mutation vocabulary and the bundled examples — is this repository's own registration contract, which no third party implements. It is stated once, language-neutrally, in `../🧫️fixtures/🧩️mount-contract/🔣️.json`; the Rust half reads the real manifests the plugin builder produces, and the TypeScript and Python halves are independent readers that check the same statement against the kind directories on disk.",
